@prefix review: <http://example.org/agora/review#> .
@prefix perception: <http://example.org/agora/perception#> .
@prefix water: <http://example.org/agora/water#> .
@prefix reporting: <http://example.org/agora/reporting#> .
@prefix ag: <http://example.org/agora#> .
@prefix market: <http://example.org/agora/market#> .

#  Fern's agent's PRIVATE beliefs — the parameters for the capabilities it composed.
#
#  Grouped by the module that reads them. A module never reads outside its own vocabulary,
#  so adding a capability means adding a block here, and nothing else changes.
#
#  Nothing here is repeated from the world: the wiring (which plant, which sensor, which
#  market) is stated once, publicly, there. This file is only what fern *thinks*.

##  perception:Subscribing — the interval it asks its board to keep
ag:fern_agent
    perception:fastSleepS 30 ;          # at/below its own low band: watch closely
    perception:slowSleepS 600 ;         # comfortable: let the board sleep, save energy
    perception:readingGraceS 45 .     # slack past the cadence it asked for, before it calls the sensor quiet

##  market:Bidding — what it aims at and what it will pay
#
#  The bands that used to sit here are gone. Where a fern is parched and where it is soaked are
#  facts about the FERN, stated in world.ttl as an operating range and a survival range, and
#  `desire:Deducing` intersects them into the region this agent holds. Restating them privately
#  meant keeping a second copy of a public fact and being free to keep a wrong one.
#
#  The target stays, because it is a PICK and not a range: the one point inside the region this
#  agent aims for, which the shapes now check against the region rather than against the plant.
ag:fern_agent
    market:hasEndowment 100.0 ;
    water:hasTarget 0.55 ;         # a pick inside 0.45-0.65, which the world states
    water:litresPerFraction 2.0 ;  # what it BELIEVES its pot takes (the world knows the truth)
    water:maxValuePerL 0.80 .      # willingness to pay at peak urgency — never disclosed

##  How often it says how it is — belief base size, reading freshness, silent write failures.
#   Omit this line and the agent reports nothing; see agora/metrics.py.
ag:fern_agent reporting:metricsIntervalS 60 .

##  Self-review — how often at the very least.
#   Required because the world gave this agent room to move (review:commits, in world.ttl): an
#   agent granted none derives no review capability and needs no interval. A FLOOR and not a
#   schedule — a decision plans its own next arising from when its effect could show.
#   See knowledge/decisions/self-review-is-a-capability.md.
ag:fern_agent review:reviewIntervalS 300 .
